  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SI-AI4STEM: AI-driven Inclusive STEM Learning for Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ2024TEA570A103
01/09/2024 - 31/08/2029
Most Tanzanian students in rural settings and those with disabilities fail to receive quality education. This leads to poor performance in STEM subjects, and slim chances to pursue STEM careers. Nevertheless, digital technologies are globally used to improve access to quality education. Thus, Mzumbe University and Ghent University aim to establish a centre for research on leveraging Artificial Intelligence (AI) to enhance children&#x2019;s learning experiences and career chances in STEM.</narrative>
  </description>
